Strained to the limit like an overdrawn bow string, the λSanngridr requires a pilot of equal sharpness to the voracity of her weapons.

Despite being equipped with top-of-the-line avionics and automation systems, the Lambda Sanngridr has the greatest training requirement of all AAM designs, owing to the general fragility of her hull, highly asymmetrical thrust profile, and extreme maneuverability.

To the general public, the full capabilities of this ship are unknown; however, based on publicly available combat footage and pictures taken of the ship by civilians at the Homecoming colony, it is believed that the ship has an extremely high TWR and likely maneuverability to match. Civilian analysts believe that the ship achieves the high turn rate while maintaining the observed acceleration by utilizing various weight-saving components, such as Prototech Gyroscopes and Reactors, which may reduce ship mass by an estimated half a million kilograms.
(citation needed)

The suspected use of prototech components and reports of mass deployments of the ship have led many civilian analysts to voice concerns regarding the potential drain on CASA's P-Tech reserves. Thus far, AAM has declined to comment on the manufacturing costs of the Lambda Sanngridr but has assured the media that the Lambda Sanngrider will be the mass-produced ship of choice to fill in the destroyer role within CASA's navy. 
